{%- comment -%}
  `media`, plus a theme asset as the middle fallback.

  Three sources, and the precedence is the same one the hero film uses:

    1. `image` — a photograph the merchant uploaded in the theme editor. Wins,
       and is the only branch that gets a responsive srcset, because `image_url`
       can resize a Shopify-hosted file and `asset_url` cannot resize anything.
    2. `asset` — a file in the theme's own assets/, shipped with the code. This
       is the branch that exists for photography that arrived as files in the
       repo rather than as an upload to the store.
    3. neither — `media`'s labelled placeholder, at the exact final size.

  WHY THIS IS A SNIPPET RATHER THAN THREE BRANCHES COPIED INTO A SECTION. It was
  written the second time a section needed it, which is the point at which
  `snippets/button.liquid` was extracted for the same reason. The asset branch is
  not one line: it has to reproduce `media`'s frame arithmetic exactly, or a
  section that falls back to an asset gets a different box from the same section
  showing its placeholder, and the layout moves when the photograph arrives. That
  arithmetic is duplicated here once, deliberately, and it is the thing to keep
  in step if `media` ever changes its frame.

  Accepts everything `media` accepts — image, asset, ratio, sizes, fill,
  priority, class, label — plus three the asset branch alone needs:

    - `alt`, because an uploaded image carries its own alt from the Files admin
      and an asset carries none at all, so the caller has to supply one.
    - `width` and `height`, which do NOT set the painted size. The img is
      `absolute inset-0 object-cover` inside a frame that already carries the
      aspect ratio, so its size comes from the frame either way; these exist
      because theme check's ImgWidthAndHeight requires them, and they should
      still be the file's real pixel dimensions rather than a pair of numbers
      that satisfies the rule. `hero-carousel.liquid` explains the same thing
      about its own pair.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign media_label = label | default: 'Photo'

  if priority
    assign loading_mode = 'eager'
    assign priority_mode = 'high'
  else
    assign loading_mode = 'lazy'
    assign priority_mode = 'auto'
  endif

  if fill
    assign box = 'absolute inset-0 h-full w-full'
    assign frame = ''
  else
    assign box = 'w-full'
    if ratio
      assign frame = 'aspect-ratio:' | append: ratio
    else
      assign frame = 'aspect-ratio:1 / 1'
    endif
  endif
-%}

{%- if image != blank -%}
  {% render 'media',
    image: image,
    ratio: ratio,
    sizes: sizes,
    fill: fill,
    priority: priority,
    class: class,
    label: media_label %}
{%- elsif asset != blank -%}
  <div style="{{ frame }}" class="relative overflow-hidden rounded-sm bg-tone {{ box }} {{ class }}">
    <img
      src="{{ asset | asset_url }}"
      alt="{{ alt | escape }}"
      width="{{ asset_width | default: 1200 }}"
      height="{{ asset_height | default: 1200 }}"
      loading="{{ loading_mode }}"
      fetchpriority="{{ priority_mode }}"
      decoding="async"
      class="absolute inset-0 h-full w-full object-cover"
    >
  </div>
{%- else -%}
  {% render 'media',
    image: nil,
    ratio: ratio,
    sizes: sizes,
    fill: fill,
    class: class,
    label: media_label %}
{%- endif -%}
